WEBVTT

00:00.810 --> 00:02.300
So in this problem
here, we're told

00:02.300 --> 00:05.350
that the triangle
ACE is isosceles.

00:05.350 --> 00:07.340
So that's this big
triangle right here.

00:07.340 --> 00:10.660
It's isosceles, which means
it has two equal sides,

00:10.660 --> 00:12.590
and we also know from
isosceles triangles

00:12.590 --> 00:15.250
that the base angles
must be equal.

00:15.250 --> 00:17.590
So these two base angles
are going to be equal.

00:17.590 --> 00:20.740
And this side right over here
is going to be equal in length

00:20.740 --> 00:21.920
to this side over here.

00:21.920 --> 00:24.790
We could say AC is
going to be equal to CE,

00:24.790 --> 00:27.590
so we get all of that
from this first statement

00:27.590 --> 00:29.090
right over there.

00:29.090 --> 00:31.400
Then they give us some
more clues, or some more

00:31.400 --> 00:32.030
information.

00:32.030 --> 00:34.120
They say CG is equal to 24.

00:34.120 --> 00:35.960
So this is CG right over here.

00:35.960 --> 00:38.020
It has length 24.

00:38.020 --> 00:43.410
They tell us BH is equal
to DF, so those two things

00:43.410 --> 00:45.010
are going to be congruent.

00:45.010 --> 00:46.640
They're going to
be the same length.

00:46.640 --> 00:50.700
Then they tell us that
GF is equal to 12.

00:50.700 --> 00:52.610
So this is GF right over here.

00:52.610 --> 00:55.210
So GF is equal to 12.

00:55.210 --> 00:57.360
That's that distance
right over there.

00:57.360 --> 01:00.910
And then finally, they tell
us that FE is equal to 6.

01:00.910 --> 01:04.330
So this is FE, and
then finally, they

01:04.330 --> 01:06.706
ask us, what is
the area of CBHFD?

01:14.420 --> 01:18.130
They're asking us for the area
of this part right over here.

01:18.130 --> 01:20.770
That part and that
part right over there.

01:20.770 --> 01:21.465
That is CBHFD.

01:23.604 --> 01:25.270
So let's think about
how we can do this.

01:25.270 --> 01:27.870
So we could figure out the
area of the larger triangle,

01:27.870 --> 01:29.410
and then from that
we could subtract

01:29.410 --> 01:31.900
the areas of these
little pieces at the end.

01:31.900 --> 01:34.510
Then, we'll be able to figure
out this middle area, this area

01:34.510 --> 01:35.260
that I've shaded.

01:35.260 --> 01:38.830
And we don't have all the
information yet to solve that.

01:38.830 --> 01:41.880
We know what the height, or the
altitude, of this triangle is,

01:41.880 --> 01:43.005
but we don't know its base.

01:43.005 --> 01:44.671
If we knew its base,
then we'd say, hey,

01:44.671 --> 01:45.612
1/2 base times height.

01:45.612 --> 01:47.070
We'd get the area
of this triangle,

01:47.070 --> 01:49.060
and then we'd have to
subtract out these areas.

01:49.060 --> 01:50.934
We don't have full
information there, either.

01:50.934 --> 01:52.260
We don't know this height.

01:52.260 --> 01:53.290
Once we know that
height, then we

01:53.290 --> 01:55.730
could figure out this height,
but we also don't quite yet

01:55.730 --> 01:58.220
know what this length
right over here is.

01:58.220 --> 02:00.590
So let's just take
it piece by piece.

02:00.590 --> 02:03.310
So the first thing we might
want to do, and you might guess,

02:03.310 --> 02:05.393
because we've been talking
a lot about similarity,

02:05.393 --> 02:07.760
is making some type of
argument about similarity

02:07.760 --> 02:10.169
here, because there's a
bunch of similar triangles.

02:10.169 --> 02:17.810
For example, triangle CGE shares
this angle with triangle DFE.

02:17.810 --> 02:20.510
They both share this
orange angle right here,

02:20.510 --> 02:23.960
and they both have this
right angle right over here.

02:23.960 --> 02:25.600
So they have two
angles in common.

02:25.600 --> 02:27.840
They're going to be
similar by angle-angle.

02:27.840 --> 02:28.700
And you can actually
show that there's

02:28.700 --> 02:30.200
going to be a third
angle in common,

02:30.200 --> 02:32.260
because these two
are parallel lines.

02:32.260 --> 02:47.150
So we can write that triangle
CGE is similar to triangle DFE,

02:47.150 --> 02:49.510
and we know that by angle-angle.

02:49.510 --> 02:52.290
We have one set of
corresponding angles congruent,

02:52.290 --> 02:54.710
and then this angle
is in both triangles,

02:54.710 --> 02:57.380
so it is a set of
corresponding congruent angles

02:57.380 --> 02:58.750
right over there.

02:58.750 --> 03:00.750
And so then, once we know
that they are similar,

03:00.750 --> 03:02.660
we can set up the
ratio between sides,

03:02.660 --> 03:05.300
because we have some information
about some of the sides.

03:05.300 --> 03:09.524
So we know that the ratio
between DF and this side

03:09.524 --> 03:11.940
right over here, which is a
corresponding side-- the ratio

03:11.940 --> 03:19.110
between DF and CG,
which is 24, is

03:19.110 --> 03:24.030
going to be the same thing as
the ratio between FE, which

03:24.030 --> 03:28.210
is 6, and GE, which is not 12.

03:28.210 --> 03:29.600
It's 12 plus 6.

03:29.600 --> 03:31.437
It is 18.

03:31.437 --> 03:32.270
And then, let's see.

03:32.270 --> 03:34.940
6 over 18, this
is just 1 over 3.

03:34.940 --> 03:42.620
You get 3DF is equal to 24.

03:42.620 --> 03:45.620
I just cross-multiplied, or
you could multiply both sides

03:45.620 --> 03:48.089
by 24, multiply both sides by 3.

03:48.089 --> 03:48.880
You would get this.

03:48.880 --> 03:51.130
Actually, you could just
multiply both sides times 24,

03:51.130 --> 03:53.550
and you'll get 24 times 1/3.

03:53.550 --> 03:55.030
But we'll just do it this way.

03:55.030 --> 03:56.240
Divide both sides by 3.

03:56.240 --> 04:00.300
You get DF is equal to 8.

04:00.300 --> 04:03.760
So we found out that DF is
equal to 8, that length right

04:03.760 --> 04:04.720
over there.

04:04.720 --> 04:06.450
And that's useful
for us because we

04:06.450 --> 04:13.140
know that this length right
over here is also equal to 8.

04:13.140 --> 04:14.760
And now what can we do?

04:14.760 --> 04:18.290
Well, it seems like we could
make another similarity

04:18.290 --> 04:20.800
argument, because we have
this angle right over here.

04:20.800 --> 04:23.860
It is congruent to that
angle right over there,

04:23.860 --> 04:25.940
and we also have
this angle, which

04:25.940 --> 04:27.140
is going to be 90 degrees.

04:27.140 --> 04:28.870
We have a 90-degree angle there.

04:28.870 --> 04:30.920
And actually, that
by itself is actually

04:30.920 --> 04:33.350
enough to say that we have
two similar triangles.

04:33.350 --> 04:34.850
We don't even have
to show that they

04:34.850 --> 04:36.190
have a congruent side here.

04:36.190 --> 04:38.565
And actually, we're going to
show that these are actually

04:38.565 --> 04:41.220
congruent triangles that we're
dealing with right over here.

04:41.220 --> 04:43.299
So we have two angles,
and actually, we

04:43.299 --> 04:44.590
could just go straight to that.

04:44.590 --> 04:46.620
Because when we talk
about congruency,

04:46.620 --> 04:49.071
if you have an angle that's
congruent to another angle,

04:49.071 --> 04:51.070
another angle that's
congruent to another angle,

04:51.070 --> 04:53.370
and then a side that's
congruent to another side,

04:53.370 --> 04:55.810
you are dealing with
two congruent triangles.

04:55.810 --> 05:00.140
So we can write-- let
me write it over here.

05:00.140 --> 05:01.700
I'll write it in pink.

05:01.700 --> 05:08.400
Triangle AHB is
congruent to-- you

05:08.400 --> 05:10.220
want to get the
corresponding vertices

05:10.220 --> 05:12.302
right-- is congruent
to triangle EFD.

05:17.870 --> 05:23.710
And we know that, because we
have angle-angle-side postulate

05:23.710 --> 05:25.320
for congruency.

05:25.320 --> 05:27.102
And if the two
triangles are congruent,

05:27.102 --> 05:28.310
that makes things convenient.

05:28.310 --> 05:30.736
That means if this side
is 8, that side is 8.

05:30.736 --> 05:31.610
We already knew that.

05:31.610 --> 05:33.318
That's how we established
our congruency.

05:33.318 --> 05:35.497
But that means if this
side has length 6,

05:35.497 --> 05:37.330
then the corresponding
side of this triangle

05:37.330 --> 05:40.060
is also going to have length 6.

05:40.060 --> 05:43.080
So we can write this
length right over here

05:43.080 --> 05:45.480
is also going to be 6.

05:45.480 --> 05:48.510
I can imagine you can imagine
where all this is going to go,

05:48.510 --> 05:50.090
but we want to
prove to ourselves.

05:50.090 --> 05:52.294
We want to know for
sure what the area is.

05:52.294 --> 05:54.960
We don't want to say, hey, maybe
this is the same thing as that.

05:54.960 --> 05:56.735
Let's just actually
prove it to ourselves.

05:56.735 --> 05:57.860
So how do we figure it out?

05:57.860 --> 06:00.276
We've almost figured out the
entire base of this triangle,

06:00.276 --> 06:03.020
but we still haven't figured
out the length of HG.

06:03.020 --> 06:05.300
Well, now we can use a
similarity argument again,

06:05.300 --> 06:08.470
because we can see that
triangle ABH is actually

06:08.470 --> 06:11.440
similar to triangle ACG.

06:11.440 --> 06:13.630
They both have this
angle here, and then

06:13.630 --> 06:16.300
they both have a right angle.

06:16.300 --> 06:18.230
ABH has a right angle there.

06:18.230 --> 06:20.130
ACG has a right angle
right over there.

06:20.130 --> 06:21.260
So you have two angles.

06:21.260 --> 06:24.470
Two corresponding angles
are equal to each other.

06:24.470 --> 06:26.730
You're now dealing
with similar triangles.

06:26.730 --> 06:33.770
So we know that triangle
ABH-- I'll just write it

06:33.770 --> 06:35.790
as AHB, since I already
wrote it this way.

06:35.790 --> 06:41.111
AHB is similar to triangle AGC.

06:41.111 --> 06:42.860
You want to make sure
you get the vertices

06:42.860 --> 06:43.651
in the right order.

06:43.651 --> 06:44.700
A is the orange angle.

06:44.700 --> 06:48.140
G is the right angle, and
then C is the unlabeled angle.

06:48.140 --> 06:51.613
This is similar to triangle AGC.

06:55.502 --> 06:56.960
And what that does
for us is now we

06:56.960 --> 07:00.910
can use the ratios to figure
out what HG is equal to.

07:00.910 --> 07:02.640
So what could we say over here?

07:02.640 --> 07:04.850
Well, we could say
that 8 over 24--

07:04.850 --> 07:07.950
BH over its corresponding
side of the larger triangle--

07:07.950 --> 07:17.856
so we say 8 over 24 is equal to
6 over not HG, but over a AG.

07:17.856 --> 07:21.700
6 over AG, and I think you
can see where this is going.

07:21.700 --> 07:23.410
You have 1/3.

07:23.410 --> 07:29.280
1/3 is equal to 6 over AG, or
we can cross-multiply here,

07:29.280 --> 07:34.450
and we can get AG
is equal to 18.

07:34.450 --> 07:37.150
So this entire length
right over here is 18.

07:37.150 --> 07:41.224
If AG is 18 and AH
is 6, then HG is 12.

07:41.224 --> 07:43.390
This is what you might have
guessed if you were just

07:43.390 --> 07:45.181
trying to guess the
answer right over here.

07:45.181 --> 07:47.100
But now we have
proven to ourselves

07:47.100 --> 07:51.180
that this base has length
of-- well, we have 18 here,

07:51.180 --> 07:52.910
and then we have
another 18 here.

07:52.910 --> 07:55.890
So it has a length of 36.

07:55.890 --> 07:59.410
So the entire base here is 36.

07:59.410 --> 08:01.099
So that is 36.

08:01.099 --> 08:02.640
And so now we can
figure out the area

08:02.640 --> 08:06.080
of the entire
isosceles triangle.

08:06.080 --> 08:10.590
So the area of
ACE is going to be

08:10.590 --> 08:18.010
equal to 1/2 times the
base, which is 36, times 24.

08:18.010 --> 08:23.780
And so this is going to be
the same thing as 1/2 times 36

08:23.780 --> 08:25.566
is 18.

08:25.566 --> 08:27.440
18 times 24.

08:27.440 --> 08:29.660
I'll just do that
over here on the top.

08:29.660 --> 08:33.360
So 18 times 24.

08:33.360 --> 08:35.950
8 times 4 is 32.

08:35.950 --> 08:39.564
1 times 4 is 4, plus 3 is 7.

08:39.564 --> 08:41.230
Then we put as 0 here,
because we're now

08:41.230 --> 08:43.309
dealing not with 2, but 20.

08:43.309 --> 08:46.860
You have 2 times 8 is 16.

08:46.860 --> 08:48.400
2 times 1 is 2, plus 1.

08:48.400 --> 08:54.060
So it's 360, and then you
have a 2, 7 plus 6 is 13.

08:54.060 --> 08:56.270
1 plus 3 is 4.

08:56.270 --> 09:00.480
So the area of ACE
is equal to 432.

09:00.480 --> 09:01.840
But we're not done yet.

09:01.840 --> 09:04.730
This area that we
care about is the area

09:04.730 --> 09:09.040
of the entire triangle
minus this area

09:09.040 --> 09:11.950
and minus this area
right over here.

09:11.950 --> 09:15.390
So what is the area of
each of these little wedges

09:15.390 --> 09:16.140
right over here?

09:16.140 --> 09:19.210
So it's going to be
1/2 times 8 times 6.

09:19.210 --> 09:22.000
So 1/2 times 8 is 4 times 6.

09:22.000 --> 09:24.900
So this is going to be
24 right over there,

09:24.900 --> 09:27.570
and this is going to be
another 24 right over there.

09:27.570 --> 09:32.250
So this is going to be equal
to 432 minus 24 minus 24,

09:32.250 --> 09:35.985
or minus 48, which
is equal to-- and we

09:35.985 --> 09:37.360
could try to do
this in our head.

09:37.360 --> 09:40.740
If we subtract 32, we're
going to get to 400.

09:40.740 --> 09:44.230
And then we're going to
have to subtract another 16.

09:44.230 --> 09:45.790
So if you subtract
10 from 400, you

09:45.790 --> 09:51.802
get to 390, so that you get to
384-- whatever the units were.

09:51.802 --> 09:54.260
If these were in meters, then
this would be meters squared.

09:54.260 --> 09:56.790
If this was centimeters, this
would be centimeters squared.

09:56.790 --> 09:57.750
Did I do that right?

09:57.750 --> 09:59.720
Let me go the other way.

09:59.720 --> 10:04.320
If I add 40 to this, 24 plus
another 8 gets me to 432.

10:04.320 --> 10:06.259
Yup, we're done.
